#
# Job worker for the web UI control plane. Replaces palwarden-jobd.service.
#
# Runs as ROOT (no s6-setuidgid, unlike config-webui): that asymmetry *is* the
# control plane's privilege split. The web UI runs as steam and can only drop
# job files into the queue; every privileged effect — applying config, cycling
# the server's s6 service, SteamCMD updates — happens here, after jobd
# re-validates the action and every parameter against its own allowlist.
#
# Not wrapped in palwarden-run-periodic (as memory-watch is): jobd has its own
# poll loop and its own flock, so it is a long-running process, not a timer.
exec palwarden-jobd
